          "content": "with the ball\b It may be intentional or unintentional, and it always precedes\npossession and control\b\nb\b Intentional touching is deliberate or intended touching\b\nc\b Forced touching results when a player’s contact with the ball is due to (i)\nan opponent blocking that player into it, or (ii) the ball being batted or\nillegally kicked into that player by an opponent\b If the touching is forced,\nthe player in question by rule has not touched the ball (Rules 6-1-4 and\n6-3-4)\nd\b When in question, a ball has not been touched on a kick or forward pass\b\nBlocking a Scrimmage Kick",
          "start_page": 38,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-131",
          "snippet": "with the ball\b It may be intentional or unintentional, and it always precedes possession and control\b b\b Intentional touching is deliberate or intended touching\b c\b Forced touching results when a play…"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 5\b Blocking a scrimmage kick is touching the kicked ball by an",
          "content": "opponent of the kicking team in an attempt to prevent the ball from crossing\nthe neutral zone (Rule 6-3-1-b)\b\n\n[PAGE 39]\nFR-36 RUlE 2 / dEFinitions",
          "start_page": 38,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-132",
          "snippet": "opponent of the kicking team in an attempt to prevent the ball from crossing the neutral zone (Rule 6-3-1-b)\b [PAGE 39] FR-36 RUlE 2 / dEFinitions"
