          "id": "mens_football-rule-133",
          "snippet": "Sidelines"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 1\b A sideline runs from end line to end line on each side of the field",
          "content": "and separates the field of play from the area that is out of bounds\b The entire\nsideline is out of bounds\b\nGoal Lines and Pylons",
          "start_page": 39,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-134",
          "snippet": "and separates the field of play from the area that is out of bounds\b The entire sideline is out of bounds\b Goal Lines and Pylons"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 2\b The goal line at each end of the field of play runs between the",
          "content": "sidelines and is part of the vertical plane that separates the end zone from the\nfield of play\b The two goal lines are 100 yards apart\b The plane of the goal line\nextends between and includes the pylons, which are out of bounds\b The entire\ngoal line is in the end zone\b A team’s goal line is that which it is defending\b\nEnd Lines",
          "start_page": 39,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-135",
          "snippet": "sidelines and is part of the vertical plane that separates the end zone from the field of play\b The two goal lines are 100 yards apart\b The plane of the goal line extends between and includes the pylo…"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 3\b An end line runs between the sidelines 10 yards behind each goal",
          "content": "line and separates the end zone from the area that is out of bounds\b The entire\nend line is out of bounds\b\nBoundary Lines",
          "start_page": 39,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-136",
          "snippet": "line and separates the end zone from the area that is out of bounds\b The entire end line is out of bounds\b Boundary Lines"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 4\b The boundary lines are the sidelines and the end lines\b The area",
          "content": "enclosed by the boundary lines is “inbounds,’’ and the area surrounding and\nincluding the boundary lines is “out of bounds\b’’\nRestraining Lines",
          "start_page": 39,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-137",
          "snippet": "enclosed by the boundary lines is “inbounds,’’ and the area surrounding and including the boundary lines is “out of bounds\b’’ Restraining Lines"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 5\b A restraining line is part of a vertical plane that limits a team’s",
          "content": "alignment for free kicks\b The plane extends beyond the sidelines (A\bR\b 2-12-\n5-I)\b\nYard Lines",
          "start_page": 39,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-138",
          "snippet": "alignment for free kicks\b The plane extends beyond the sidelines (A\bR\b 2-12- 5-I)\b Yard Lines"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 6\b A yard line is any line in the field of play parallel to the end lines\b",
          "content": "A team’s own yard lines, marked or unmarked, are numbered consecutively\nfrom its own goal line to the 50-yard line\b\nHash Marks",
          "start_page": 39,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-139",
          "snippet": "A team’s own yard lines, marked or unmarked, are numbered consecutively from its own goal line to the 50-yard line\b Hash Marks"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 7\b The two hash marks are 60 feet from the sidelines\b Hash marks",
          "content": "and short yard-line extensions shall measure 24 inches in length\b\nNine-Yard Marks",
          "start_page": 39,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-140",
          "snippet": "and short yard-line extensions shall measure 24 inches in length\b Nine-Yard Marks"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 8\b Nine-yard marks 12 inches in length, every 10 yards, shall be",
