          "snippet": "Kicking the Ball; Legal and Illegal Kicks"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 1\b a\b Kicking the ball is intentionally striking the ball with the knee,",
          "content": "lower leg or foot\b\nb\b A legal kick is a punt, drop kick or place kick made according to the rules\nby a player of Team A before a change of team possession\b Kicking the ball\nin any other manner is illegal (A\bR\b 6-1-2-I)\b\nc\b Any free kick or scrimmage kick continues to be a kick until it is caught or\nrecovered by a player or becomes dead\b\nd\b When in question, a ball is accidentally touched rather than kicked\b\nPunt",
          "start_page": 40,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-149",
          "snippet": "lower leg or foot\b b\b A legal kick is a punt, drop kick or place kick made according to the rules by a player of Team A before a change of team possession\b Kicking the ball in any other manner is ille…"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 2\b A punt is a kick by a player who drops the ball and kicks it before",
