          "content": "or successful field goal attempt (Exception: In extra periods)\b It must be a place\nkick or a drop kick\b\nScrimmage Kick",
          "start_page": 41,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-154",
          "snippet": "or successful field goal attempt (Exception: In extra periods)\b It must be a place kick or a drop kick\b Scrimmage Kick"
        },
        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 7\b a\b A scrimmage kick is a punt, drop kick, or field goal place kick\b",
          "content": "It is a legal kick if it is made by Team A in or behind the neutral zone during\na scrimmage down before team possession changes\b\nb\b A scrimmage kick has crossed the neutral zone when it touches the ground,\na player, an official or anything beyond the neutral zone (Exception: Rule\n6-3-1-b) (A\bR\b 6-3-1-I-IV)\b\nc\b A scrimmage kick made when the kicker’s entire body and the ball is or\nhas been beyond the neutral zone is an illegal kick and a live-ball foul that\ncauses the ball to become dead (Rule 6-3-10-c)\b\nReturn Kick",
          "start_page": 41,
          "id": "mens_football-rule-155",
          "snippet": "It is a legal kick if it is made by Team A in or behind the neutral zone during a scrimmage down before team possession changes\b b\b A scrimmage kick has crossed the neutral zone when it touches the gr…"
