        {
          "title": "ARTICLE 1\b There shall be no unsportsmanlike conduct or any act that",
          "content": "interferes with orderly game administration on the part of players, substitutes,\ncoaches, authorized attendants or any other persons subject to the rules, before\nthe game, during the game or between periods\b Infractions for these acts by\nplayers are administered as either live-ball or dead-ball fouls depending on when\nthey occur\b (A\bR\b 9-2-1-I-X)\na\b Specifically prohibited acts and conduct include:\n1\b No player, substitute, coach or other person subject to the rules shall\nuse abusive, threatening or obscene language or gestures, or engage in\nsuch acts that provoke ill will or are demeaning to an opponent, to\ngame officials or to the image of the game, including but not limited\nto:\n(a) Pointing the finger(s), hand(s), arm(s) or ball at an opponent, or\nimitating the slashing of the throat\b\n\n[PAGE 106]",
