          "title": "Rule 1-2-h-4: This diagram is intended to provide clarity regarding the rules",
          "content": "governing field markings and logo placement\b The use of commercial logos\nin the field is permissible in no more than three locations (midfield and two\nflanking locations)\b These three locations are inclusive of both the commercial\nnaming rights allowance and the permissive rule that was passed in advance\nof the 2024 playing season to align regular-season rules with neutral-site and\npostseason rules\b Previously approved, Rule 1-2-h-3 allows a commercial entity\nor individual that has purchased naming rights to advertise on two of the\nflanking logos on the field\b Of note, a maximum of two of the flanking logos\nmay be used for advertising in any form\b\n\n[PAGE 139]\nFR-136 aPPEndix d / FiEld diaGRams\nGOAL POST DETAIL PYLON DETAIL\nRECOMMENDED YARD-LINE END ZONE DETAIL\nNUMBERING\n\n[PAGE 140]",
