        {
          "title": "Appendix I - Accommodations for Student-Athletes with Disabilities ��177",
          "content": "Index to Rules ��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������178\n3\n\n[PAGE 7]\nNCAA Softball\nRules Committee\nThe chart below lists the members of the committee who voted on and\napproved the rules included in this edition of the book� This information is\nbeing included for historical purposes�\nName Institution Term Expiration\nKelsey Christensen Providence College 8-31-28\nBecky Clark University of South Alabama 8-31-27\nMarie Curran-Headley State University of New York at 8-31-28\nCobleskill\nFelicia Johnson Virginia State University 8-31-28\nTina Phillips, chair University of Pittsburgh, 8-31-26\nBradford\nVickie Van Kleeck* Secretary-Rules Editor 8-31-27\nTim Walton University of Florida 8-31-27\nBetsy Wilcox Southeast Missouri State 8-31-28\nUniversity\nJoe Yegge Montana State University 8-31-28\nBillings\n*Non-voting member\nFor a complete and current listing of the NCAA Softball Rules Committees,\nplease go to www.ncaa.org/playingrules�\nContact information for the secretary-rules editor, national coordinator of\numpires and equipment consultant is available on Page 10�\n4\n\n[PAGE 8]\nMajor Rules Changes for\n2026 and 2027\nEach changed or altered segment is identified in the rules by a shaded background.\nBases - First Base (Rules 2.7.2, 12.6 and 12.11.8). Requires the use of the\ndouble first base beginning with the 2026 season for Division I and the 2027\nseason for Divisions II and III�\nSignal Arm Band (Rule 3.10.8). Allows players to wear their signal arm band/\ndevice on their arm, belt, in their pocket, etc� Note: Pitchers may not wear it on\ntheir pitching arm�\nElectronic Equipment (Rule 5.9.9). Allows an exclusively one-way electronic\ncommunication device to be used on offense and for signals to be transmitted from\nthe dugout of coaches' boxes on the field�\nVideo Review - Challenges (Rule 5.9.10 and Appendix G). Allows a head\ncoach to retain their video review challenge if the ruling is changed�\nVideo Review - Plays Subject to Review (Rule 5.9.10 and Appendix G).\nRevises video review�\nVideo Review - Criteria (Rule 5.9.10 and Appendix G). Allows teams to\ncongregate during a video review without being charged with a conference�\nProtests (Rule 7.2). Requires all protests to be resolved during the game�\nReentry (Rule 8.6.2.2). Expands the reentry rules to include any medical\ncondition with the potential to cause catastrophic injury or illness, as determined\nby a primary athletics health care provider�\nObstruction (Rule 9.5.2). Clarifies obstruction�\nTime Allowed Between Pitches (Rules 10.18 and 11.2.1). Requires the\nbatter and catcher to be in their respective boxes within 12 seconds�\nScoreboards and Video (Appendix F). Allows an unlimited number of replays\non the in-venue scoreboard/videoboard, at any speed, while a play is under video\nreview by the umpires�\nPreviously Approved Rules Change Effective with the 2027 Season\nFences (Rule 2.15.1). By January 1, 2027, requires sideline and home run\nfences constructed of a hard material to be padded� Approved Summer 2022�\n5\n\n[PAGE 9]\nSignificant Editorial\nChanges\nNote: These are additions/clarifications that have been part of case book interpretations\nor custom but have not appeared in the rules book. There have been many minor\neditorial changes to clean up language and eliminate wordiness.\nRule.....................................................Change\n5.2�������������������������������������������������������Clarification\n6.2.2 Note�����������������������������������������Interpretation\n6.6.5����������������������������������������������������Clarification\n7.1.1.2.5����������������������������������������������Clarification\n7.2.5.2�������������������������������������������������Clarification\n8.3.2 EFFECT(a) Note�����������������������Clarification\n8.3.3.5.3 EFFECT Note 3������������������Clarification\n10.18���������������������������������������������������Clarification\n12.11.12����������������������������������������������Clarification",
