dd language regarding the use of official video and confirmation�\n6-2 Failure to Participate rule has been modified to apply to all\nscored competitions�\n6-4�5 Outline stricter specifications on all shoes worn in competition�\n7-5�2b In races on a curve, steps on or over the curb or line to the\nleft with more than one step throughout the entirety of the race�\n7-9, 7-10 Reorganize the formation of heat, sections, lane assignments,\nstarting positions and qualifying�\n8-2�2 The crossbar shall be initially raised in increments of five (5)\ncentimeters�\n8-3�2 The crossbar shall be initially raised in increments of fifteen\n(15) centimeters�\nPart II - Outdoor Track and Field\nRule Change\n12-2,12-3, Redefine the roles of Meet Management (formerly Games\n12-4 Committee), Meet Director and Referee�\n12-6 Language added for the competition manager�\n13-7 Changed the language of an immediate protest to a\nchallenge� Defined who can submit a challenge and when a\nchallenge is allowed�\n13-8 Add language regarding the use of official video and confirmation�\n14-2 Failure to Participate rule has been modified to apply to all\nscored competitions�\n14-4�5 Outline stricter specifications on all shoes worn in competition�\n15-5�2b In races on a curve, steps on or over the curb or line to the\nleft with more than one step throughout the entirety of the\nrace� In races on a curve, steps on or over the curb or line to\n5\n\n[PAGE 9]\n6 Major rules Changes for 2025 and 2026\nthe left with more than one step throughout the entirety of\nthe race�\n15-9,15-10 Reorganize the formation of heat, sections, lane assignments,\nstarting positions and qualifying�\n16-2�2 The crossbar shall be initially raised in increments of five (5)\ncentimeters�\n16-3�2 The crossbar shall be initially raised in increments of fifteen\n(15) centimeters�\nPart III - Cross Country\nRule Change\n20-2,20-3,20-4 Redefine the roles of Meet Management (formerly\nGames Committee), Meet Director and Referee�\n21-8 Add language regarding the use of official video and confirmation�\n22-3�5 Outline stricter specifications on all shoes worn in competition�\n\n[PAGE 10]\nSignificant Editorial\nChanges\nThese are additions/clarifications/deletions to the rules book. Some have been part of\npast interpretations or custom, while others are minor editorial changes to clean up\nlanguage and eliminate wordiness.\nPart I - Indoor Track and Field\nRule Explanation\nChanged the term Games Committee to Meet Management\nthroughout the rules book�\n2-1�6 Returning language that, as of December 1, 2018, all newly\nconstructed or resurfaced tracks shall be surveyed for a curb\nand shall have a regulation curb in place for competition�\n7-7�1 Four unique competitors of the same gender constitute a\nrelay team, each of whom (except in shuttle relays) carries a baton�\nPart II - Outdoor Track and Field\nRule Explanation\nChanged the term Games Committee to Meet Management\nthroughout the rules book�\n13-1�5 The Heptathlon / Decathlon consists of seven events that\nshall be held on two consecutive 24-hour periods in the\nfollowing order:\n15-1�5 Four unique competitors of the same gender constitute a\nrelay team, each of whom (except in shuttle relays) carries a baton�\nPart III - Cross Country\nRule Explanation\n17-11 A penalty for a violation of the playing rules in which a\ncompetitor is prohibited from further competing in the race�\nThe result of the race by the competitor shall be recorded as DQ�\n17-22 The term pistol, as used within these rules, encompasses all\ndevices used to start or recall a race� A firing or a discharge\nis the activation of such a device� A pistol cannot fire live\nammunition�\n7\n\n[PAGE 11]",
