          "title": "ARTICLE 1� When engaged in competition, each competitor must wear an",
          "content": "official school-issued team uniform that consists of two components, a top\nand a bottom� A one-piece body suit is acceptable as a combination of the two\ncomponents�\n\n[PAGE 155]\n152 rule 14 / the CoMpetitors\na� Competitors who are not in proper uniform compliance will not be allowed to\ncomplete until a compliant uniform is worn�\n1) The competition shall not be delayed to accommodate compliance with\nthe rule�\nb� On any single day of competition, all team members must wear uniforms of\nthe same color or combination (e�g�, white top, red bottom)�\n1) Teams may change uniform colors from one day to another for multiple\nday meets�\n2) Men’s and women’s programs from the same institution are separate teams,\nand are not required to have uniforms of identical color�\nO 3) If a one-piece body suit is worn it shall be of the same color as the top worn\nby other members of the institution’s team\nU c� Competitors on the same team are not required to wear the same style of\nuniform�\nT d� The uniform top must, by design and size, cover the full length of the\ntorso, meeting or hanging below the waistband of the bottoms, while the\nD competitor is standing, and allow for meet management-issued identification\nto be placed above the waist, front and back�\nO 1) Uniform tops must be worn so to not obscure hip numbers�\n2) Additional visible clothing is an undergarment� It must be worn under the\nO uniform and be of a solid color�\ne� Competitors shall not use or wear artificial noisemakers�\nR f� Wearing any part of the official team competition uniform illegally (that is,\ntop off or intentionally shortened, shoulder straps lowered) while in the area\nof competition shall lead to a warning by the nearest official and a report\nof uncorrected violations shall be made to meet management, referee and\noffending competitor’s coach\nNote 1: Uniforms, meet management issued identification and shoe compliance rules\nshall be enforced through inspection b