          "content": "O Role\nThe role of meet management, is to organize and oversee all aspects of the entire\nO\nmeet� If no meet management staff is established, all responsibilities become the\nduties of the meet director� Responsibilities include:\nR\na� Appoint a meet director�\nb� Assist the meet director with meet administration�\nc� Determine the number, selection and assignments of competition officials;\n1) Inform officials and prepare officials’ materials;\n2) Appoint a jury of appeals if deemed appropriate;\n3) Provide for pertinent officials to remain at the competition site until the\nend of any protest period;\nd� Determine meet procedures;\n1) The entry process for the competition;\n2) The entry deadline for the competition;\n3) The number of competitors allowed in each event;\n4) The number of competitors an institution is allowed in each event;\n5) The use, type and placement of competitor identification;\n6) A time schedule and order of events for the meet;\n7) Reporting times for competitors in all events;\n8) The ranked order of preferred lanes and alleys for each event that assign a\nstarting position in a lane or alley;\n9) Entry standards, if applicable;\n10) The procedures and location for filing a protest, including any fees that\nmay be assessed;\n11) Qualifying procedures and drawing for lanes;\n12) Procedures to resolve ties for the last qualifying position in subsequent\nrounds;\n13) The use of implements for the competition;\n14) The time, place and location for inspecting, weighing and measuring all\nimplements to be used in the competition;\n15) The number of field event competitors who will advance to the final\nround;\n16) The number of flights in field events and group field event competitors;\n17) Starting heights and increments for the vertical jump events;\n18) The use of facilities for and the conduct of Combined Events;\n19) Determine video equipment and provider that can be used for official\nvideo review by the referee and/or jury of appeals prior to the start of the\ncompetition;\n20) Determine video equipment and provider that can be used by field event\nofficials to confirm a fair or foul attempt in the horizontal jumps and throws;\n21) The use of the start information system; and\n22) Publish prior to the meet the location and method of obtaining the\nofficial results of each event (i�e�, scoreboard, physical printout or online)�\ne� Provide full and early meet information to all competing schools, including\nentry marks;\n\n[PAGE 42]\nI\nN",
