          "title": "ARTICLE 5� Competitors may compete in bare feet or with shoes on one or",
          "content": "both feet� The purpose of shoes for competition is to protect and stabilize the\nfeet and provide a firm grip on the ground� Such shoes must be constructed to\ngive a competitor no unfair additional advantage� Incorporating any technology\nand/or device in the shoe’s construction that artificially enhances a competitor’s\nperformance is not permitted� Any type of shoe must be listed on the World\nAthletics approved list�\nCustomizations are only permissible in accordance with Regulation 7 of the\nAthletic Shoe Regulations for medical/safety reasons and need WA approval�\n\n[PAGE 157]\n154 rule 14 / the CoMpetitors\nThe sole of the shoe (including the part beneath the competitor’s heel) may\nbe constructed as to provide for the use of up to 11 spikes� Features on, and\npart of, the sole and/or heel (grooves, ridges, indentations or protuberances) are\npermissible if constructed of the same or similar material as the sole�\nWhen a competition is conducted on a synthetic surface, the part of each spike\nthat projects beyond the plane where the sole or heel touches the surface must\nnot exceed 9 millimeters, except in the High Jump, in which it must not exceed\n12 millimeters� Spikes shall have a maximum diameter of 4 millimeters for the\none-half of their total length closest to the tip� Facility considerations may further\nlimit the type of spikes allowed�\nFor all field events, the sole at the center of the athlete’s forefoot must not be\nO\nhigher than the sole at the center of the athlete’s heel�\nThe maximum thickness of individual event shoe soles are as follows:\nU\nFor all field events except triple jumps - 20mm;\nT For triple jump - 20mm;\nFor track events (including hurdle events) up to but not including 800\nD meters - 20mm;\nFor track events 800m and above (including steeplechase events) - 20mm;\nO For relay events the rule applies to the distance of the leg being run by\neach athlete�\nO Athletes may not use appliances, either inside 