          "content": "Index to Women's Basketball Rules ������������������������������������������������������������130\n1\n\n[PAGE 7]\nNCAA Women’s Basketball\nRules Committee\nThe chart below lists the members of the committee who voted on and\napproved the rules included in this edition of the book� This information is\nbeing included for historical purposes�\nName Institution or Conference Term Expiration\nTricia Binford Montana State University 8-31-24\nNicki Collen Baylor University 8-31-26\nChris Cross Cedarville University 8-31-26\nCarol Jue Chapman University 8-31-26\nAlex Lang Brooklyn College 8-31-24\nJon Levinson* Secretary-Rules Editor 8-31-26\nAlan Nakamura Biola University 8-31-23\nKelcey Roegiers Georgia State University 8-31-23\nDiane Thompson Colorado Christian 8-31-26\nUniversity\nTiffany Tucker University of North 8-31-25\nCarolina Wilmington\nAmy Vachon, chair University of Maine 8-31-23\nDebbie Williamson Atlantic Coast Conference 8-31-26\n* Non-voting member\nFor a complete and current listing of the NCAA Women’s Basketball\nRules Committee, please go to: www.ncaa.org/playingrules.\n2\n\n[PAGE 8]\n2023-24 and 2024-25\nWomen’s Basketball Rules\nChanges\nEach changed or altered segment is identified in the rules text by a blue-shaded\nbackground.\nRestricted Area. (Rules 1-8.1, 4-26, 10-4.7, and 10-10.15). Redefines the\nrestricted area to the area directly underneath each basket and eliminates the\nlower defensive box� Prohibits a defender from obtaining legal guarding position\nunderneath the basket�\nShot-Clock Displays. (Rule 1-19.4). Permits an amber light strip at the top\nof the backboard only to signify the end of a shot-clock period�\nUniforms and Player Equipment. (Rules 1-22 and 1-25.7). (In summary)\nProvides for other identifying names as approved by the institution, numbers 0\nor 00 through 99, and permits the use of religious headwear without a waiver\nprovided it is safe for competition�\nTobacco Prohibition. (Rules 2-4.4, 10-14.1.a.7, and 10-14.1.b.5). By\ndirective of the Playing Rules Oversight Panel, the former Appendix II, which\nprohibited the possession and use of tobacco products by officials, players, and\nbench personnel, has been moved into the playing rules�\nOfficial’s Duties - 10-Second Backcourt Count. (Rule 2-7.9). Require\nofficials to use the game clock to administer the 10-second backcourt count when\nthe shot clock is not visible�\nDuties of the Shot-Clock Operator. (Rule 2-11.6.c.3). The shot clock\nwill reset to 20 seconds or the time remaining on the shot clock when a foul is\ncommitted by the non-shooting team in the shooting team’s frontcourt during an\nunsuccessful field-goal or free-throw attempt that does not strike the ring or flange\nbut is not committed against a player in the act of shooting or an airborne shooter�",
