          "title": "Section 4. Guidelines for Officiating Intentional and Disqualifying",
          "content": "Fouls\nWhen determining whether a foul is to be ruled an intentional or disqualifying\nfoul due to the level of contact caused, the officials are to consider:\na� The severity of the contact caused by the fouler;\nb� Whether the fouler's contact may be considered a legitimate basketball play;\nNote: A foul that is considered a legitimate basketball play may still be ruled an\nintentional or disqualifying foul if other criteria are applicable.\nc� When the fouler commits a foul with their arm or hand, whether they wind\nup prior to contact or follow through after making contact;\nd� The severity of any injury suffered by the offended player; and\ne� The outcome of the contact (i�e�, does the contact lead to an altercation or\nfight)�\n\n[PAGE 117]",
